  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-8-1999-p3.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "We have that A is the same as \\[ \\dfrac{3}{6} + \\dfrac{2}{6} + \\dfrac{1}{6} = 1. \\]\n\nB reduces to \\[ 2 - 2 + 1 = 1. \\]\n\nC adds up to \\[ 0.1 + 0.3 + 0.6 = 1. \\]\n\nD however adds to \\[ 1.1 - 2.1 + 1.0 = 0. \\]\n\nTo make sure, we check that E has a sum of \\[ -\\dfrac{8}{2} + 5 = 5 - 4 = 1. \\]\n\nThus, D is the correct answer.",
      "hints": [
        "Compute the easiest-looking sums first",
        "Only one listed triplet fails to total \\(1\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
